WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:16.410
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.860
Okay, lunch is ready.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:21.120
Today we're having a simmered 
soup and freshly baked bread.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.930
Thanks for always cooking, Mina. Let's eat.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.550
Mina, this is good.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.300
I'm glad. Our lunch break 
isn't long, so eat quickly.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.260
You should take a break, too.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.840
I will, once I've finished washing 
the teacups we use for guests.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.970
Master, someone's staring at me.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.380
Yeah, they sure are.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.310
Wow, she really is a beast, 
just like Dad said!

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.040
She's a beast girl!

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.940
Her tail is so fluffy.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.180
Her ears twitch, too. I wanna touch them.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.320
Ms. Noela!

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:56.920
Woof...

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.920
Wait, aren't these Mr. Alf's kids?

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.450
Master, they're touching me.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:11.000
Sorry, guys. This beast girl 
doesn't like being touched.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.630
You can pet this instead.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.670
What? That thing?

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:15.960
Just a tail?

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.740
But it's fluffy.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.240
So this is what you were working 
on last night, Mr. Reiji.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.560
You can make handicrafts in 
addition to medicines. Impressive.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.520
I like this better!

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.580
Me, too!

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.260
<i>My Noela substitute plan failed.</i>

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.490
<i>I'll have to make a 
full-body substitute next.</i>

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.700
Let me take a crack at it.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.160
Everyone, would you like something to eat?

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.830
That looks yummy!

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:47.830
I'm saved.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.200
Thanks, Mina.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:56.010
<i>I need to give Mina a break 
now and then. All right.</i>

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.310
<b>Drugstore</b>

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.310
<b>In Another World</b>

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.930
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 1
 Dishwashing Detergent Scrubba-dub-dub</b>

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:34.420
Mr. Reiji, this new medicine is amazing.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.940
I hardly scrubbed at all, 
but the plates are magically clean.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.900
It just takes a scrubba-dub-dub.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.800
You said it's called "detergent"?

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.120
That's great. Sounds like 
it was worth making.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.290
With this detergent, I think 
I might even enjoy washing dishes.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.460
I'll do the dishes, though.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.460
What? You will?

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.420
You don't need to cook today, either.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.960
I'm always relying on you to do everything.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.880
You need to rest sometimes.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.290
Then who will cook?

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.090
Hold on.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:04.740
Noela, let's go.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.890
Oh, right.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:08.520
I'll need this.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.680
<b>Rabbit Tavern</b>

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.040
Excuse me.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:15.590
I'm here for the boxed lunches I ordered. 
I'm from Kirio Drugstore.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:18.400
Ah, you mean the apothecary 
on the edge of town.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.860
<b>Rena</b>

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.860
I'll wrap them right now. One moment, please.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:26.760
Woof!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.710
Thanks for the help.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.030
You're the one helping me.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:32.990
Huh? Did I do something for you?

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:33.580
You made that.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.040
<b>Botanical
Deodorant</b>

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.040
No matter how much I cleaned, 
the smell wouldn't go away.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.510
But your botanical deodorant 
was immediately effective.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.300
Oh, you bought that? If you'd 
like, you can try using this.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.100
Is this a new medicine?

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:52.100
It makes washing dishes much easier.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.850
It's still a prototype, though.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.170
You have medicine for that, 
too? I'll use it right away.

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.560
Thank you.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.570
Hey, you.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:04.240
Are you the guy who made the super potion 
that's popular in town right now?

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.240
Huh?

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.970
<b>Doz</b>

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:06.150
You got a minute?

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.450
<b>Moz</b>

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.450
Got a minute?

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.650
What? Y-You want to talk to me?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:12.060
I sense a fight. I'll protect you, Master.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.700
Doz, Moz, cut it out.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.930
But Captain...

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:19.360
I'm tellin' ya to cut it out.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.670
<b>Annabelle</b>

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:20.980
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.020
Woof, woof. I won!

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:27.310
Noela, that's not what 
happened. Who are they?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.760
The Red Cat Brigade.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.720
<b>Red Cat Brigade</b>

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.790
Red Cat Brigade?

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:33.930
Cats?

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:37.960
They're a mercenary company hired 
by the lord to protect this town.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.100
That woman is their captain.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.020
She's the captain of a 
mercenary company?

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.740
Sorry about that, apothecary.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:49.050
Oh, don't worry about it. 
A-Anyway, let's go, Noela.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:49.570
Woof.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.450
See you later.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.630
I can't take it anymore!

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:54.660
Can't take it anymore!

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.830
Hey, you two!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.130
<i>Wait, am I being followed?</i>

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:03.800
Hey, stop!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.510
Stop!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.130
O-Okay!

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.600
Hey, apothecary!

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:07.720
Apothecary!

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.380
I mean, Sir Apothecary, I'm beggin' ya.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.510
I-I'm beggin' ya.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:14.720
Huh?

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:20.900
Could you deliver five of yer super potions 
to our barracks each day for half price?

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.150
C-Could you?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.290
What do you think yer doin'?!

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.490
But Captain, you can't survive 
without them potions.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:32.320
Th-That's not true.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.170
Everybody knows.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:35.440
We know.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:39.000
We know you secretly drink the 
potions we have stashed every night.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:43.330
There's always at least two missin', 
sometimes all five when it's real bad.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:45.000
We count 'em every mornin'.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.210
It's not me.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.090
There's no point in hidin' it.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.560
That's why we're negotiatin' 
with the apothecary

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:54.290
to sell us potions cheap fer you!

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.650
Doz is right!

00:06:55.650 --> 00:07:00.280
What belongs to the Red Cat Brigade 
is mine, and what's mine is mine, too!

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.150
Quit yer whining!

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:04.310
<i>I see nonsensical logic 
exists in this world, too.</i>

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:09.190
Then what belongs to my master is 
mine, and what's mine is mine, too.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.040
You don't need to remember that.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:15.050
Captain, the Red Cat Brigade is currently 
facin' serious money problems.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.580
Whose fault do you think that is?

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.160
It's because we don't get paid enough.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.580
No, it's your fault!

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.880
S-So... you wanted five potions 
delivered daily, right?

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:26.300
Huh?

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.710
Oh, you don't need to pay for them.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:32.130
You mean they're free?! Yer a god!

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.850
Huh?! No, I'm just an apothecary...

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:39.440
I-If you insist, I suppose we'd 
be willin' to accept 'em.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.630
Sorry she's not more honest, god of medicine.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.020
Our captain is actually real happy.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.270
She's happy.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.730
I told you, I'm not a god.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.200
I am honest, and I ain't happy.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.070
You sure you're willin' 
to give 'em away fer free?

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.740
In that case, I do have one request.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.750
Whatever you wish, medicine god.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.360
Whatever you wish.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.560
<b>Rabbit Tavern Kitchen</b>

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:03.700
You want us to use this 
detergent to wash dishes?

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:04.500
Yes.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:09.240
If you enjoy using it, 
tell everyone in Kalta about it.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:12.220
The sales will cover the 
cost of your potions.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:12.900
Got—

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:16.520
Got it. I shall wash these 
dishes as you command.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.210
No, I shall wash them!

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:18.600
No, me!

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.700
No, me!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.020
Cut it out, you two! I'm gonna handle this one!

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.280
Go right ahead.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:24.740
<i>What is this?</i>

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:27.490
Captain, please use this.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.460
O-Oh, thanks.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.500
L-Like this?

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.740
Yes. Try lathering it up.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.990
What is this?!

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.790
That's how it works. It's fine.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.590
You're right. Incredible.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.450
It's so bubbly and fluffy. Right, Captain?

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.500
Y-Yeah.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:48.540
M-Makin' the captain wash dishes 
kinda feels like a guilty pleasure.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.960
Yeah. It's kinda excitin'.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:54.040
Captain, you can stop washing that one.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.550
It's already clean.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.010
Don't make me laugh.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.570
There's no way this dish got 
clean in such a short—

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:03.910
It did?! It's actually clean?!

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.270
What a great reaction.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.980
Did the captain use magic?

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.900
I didn't do nothin'.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.070
Which means it was the 
work of the medicine god!

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:16.030
I-I told you, I'm not a god. 
That's just how this medicine works.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.600
I can't believe how easy 
it makes washing dishes.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.100
My hands don't even wrinkle.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.000
Huh... I might be able handle this.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.880
What? Have the captain's housekeepin' 
abilities been awakened?

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:28.420
The medicine god's new medicine 
is somethin' to be feared!

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:31.500
Please stop that, seriously.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.090
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.090
Really? That's what happened?

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:39.490
Yeah, so we have to deliver five potions to 
the Red Cat Brigade every day from now on.

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:41.180
Noela, could you handle the deliveries?

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.100
Woof. You can count on me.

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:46.940
Ms. Noela, don't drink 
them on your way there.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:50.910
What belongs to my master is mine, 
and what's mine is mine, too.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:52.400
What does that mean?

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:52.400
Oh, that's just...

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.360
<i>She learned a phrase she didn't 
need to know from that captain.</i>

00:09:56.770 --> 00:10:00.370
Mr. Reiji and Ms. Noela,
I got plenty of rest today.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.030
Thank you.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.090
Woof.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:04.120
I'm glad to hear that.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.050
But please let me cook.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:08.970
I had nothing to do while I waited.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.900
It actually made me more weary.

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:12.250
Huh? Is that how that works?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:16.680
Yes. Since it doesn't take as long to wash 
the dishes now, I've got plenty of time.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:20.170
All thanks to your Scrubba-dub-dub 
dishwashing detergent.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:24.810
<b>Dishwashing 
Detergent
Scrubba-dub-dub</b>

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:21.970
"Scrubba-dub-dub"?

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.800
I named it.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.560
<b>Red Cat Brigade Barracks</b>

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:34.150
I can't wait any longer!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.110
Here, Noela. This potion's for you.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:40.070
Master's potions are delicious.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.890
Don't drink the ones you're delivering.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.910
Woof. I'll be back soon.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.960
See you later, Ms. Noela.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:48.290
We're counting on you, Noela.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:50.790
What is it? Oh.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:54.950
Good morning, Captain. 
We were just on our way to you.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.550
H-Hey. I just happened to be passin' by.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.470
<i>It's awfully early in the morning for that.</i>

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:03.140
As long as I'm here, I thought 
I'd pick up my delivery.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:04.310
Woof.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.100
Thanks.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:08.280
Captain, you must really like those.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.810
One of my girls loves them, too.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:13.530
Master's potions are delicious! Delicious!

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:16.610
My name's A-Anna—

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:17.440
Anna?

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:21.150
My name's Annabelle.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.570
Ms. Annabelle. My name is Reiji.

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:29.080
I-I see. From now on, I'll 
come get them every morning.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.290
See ya later, Reiji.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:36.950
Ms. Annabelle is so nice to come 
all the way here to pick them up.

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:38.390
Nice?

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.380
Yeah, maybe she is.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:47.180
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 2
Beast-Be-Gone</b>

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.200
I can't believe there are so few herbs left.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.400
Noela, what do you think of this situation?

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:53.400
It's not good.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:58.190
You're right. It's our fault for picking 
all the herbs we wanted.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:11:59.970
We need to do something about this.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:07.910
<b>Tougirisou Seeds</b>

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.190
<i>Tougirisou seeds.</i>

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:07.910
<i>Produces yellow flowers. The leaves and 
stems can be used to make medicines.</i>

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.290
That's it!

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.710
Noela, could you gather these?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.730
Seeds? Got it. I'll gather them.

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.730
I'll gather all the seeds, woof!

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.370
What's next?

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.720
Please, Mr. Zeral!

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:24.800
Woof.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.590
Please, raise your heads.

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.640
You did a lot for us, Mr. Reiji.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:33.010
Feel free to use the Alonzo family's fields.

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:33.600
Absolutely.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:37.900
Thank you! How much should 
I pay you each month to use them?

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:41.600
I can't accept money from you 
after what you did for us.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:45.390
In exchange, I hope you'll advise me 
if anything comes up in the future.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:48.840
I'd be happy to give you 
all the advice you need.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.270
I knew I could count on 
the Alonzo family's fields!

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.540
The soil is so fertile!

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:56.540
<b>Soil Fertility
 Maximum</b>

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.210
Noela, let's plant some seeds.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:01.480
Woof! Planting time!

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:07.960
All done!

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:10.650
Mr. Reiji, are you finished?

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.610
Yes. I'll be back tomorrow to check on them.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:14.970
I see.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:16.550
Huh? Is something the matter?

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:19.110
Is Ms. Feris behaving strangely again?!

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:24.070
It's not that. There's actually something 
I forgot to tell you earlier.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.240
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.240
The crops are being ravaged?

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:31.830
Yeah. They've been suffering damage 
all over the place recently.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.700
I don't know if it's wild 
dogs or wolves or what.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.790
Why did you look at me, Master?

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:41.380
Then if you grow your herbs there, 
it's possible that they'll be ravaged.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:45.590
Even if they build fences around 
their fields, they still get inside.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.480
Then what shall we do?

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.960
It's okay. I have an idea.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.210
I'll help!

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:55.140
No, it's better if you don't come today.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.560
Woof?

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.520
<b>Utsubo Flower</b>

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:58.520
<i>Utsubo flower.</i>

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:03.570
<i>A flower that produces an unpleasant smell 
only monsters and beasts can detect.</i>

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.270
What's wrong, Ms. Noela?

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.080
Master stinks.

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:19.190
What?! Mr. Reiji, you need to bathe properly!

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.830
Ms. Noela's nose is very sensitive!

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:25.820
<b>Several Days Later</b>

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:32.660
Mr. Reiji, what did you do?

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:35.010
That dog collapsed over there.

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.810
I applied this to the fences.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:42.980
<b>Beast Repellent</b>

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.270
<i>Beast repellent.</i>

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.980
<i>A medicine that produces a smell 
offensive to beasts and monsters.</i>

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:45.190
This beast repell—

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:47.030
It'll never sell with a name like that.

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:50.040
I came up with a better one.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.240
I call it...

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:53.970
"Beast-Be-Gone."

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.600
<b>Beast Repellent</b>

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.160
<b>Beast-Be-Gone</b>

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:58.300
Actually, it's called "Beast-Be-Gone."

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:01.120
It's a medicine that produces a smell 
offensive to beasts and monsters.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:05.920
Impressive, Mr. Reiji. It only 
took you one day to make this.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:07.840
There.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:12.070
It really does keep beasts away!

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:15.550
Mr. Reiji, this is the kind of simple 
barrier that only wizards can create!

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:17.830
You've created a barrier!

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:19.640
Personal space! Also, all 
I made was a medicine...

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.110
I knew you could do it, friend!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.020
Personal space!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.980
Noela!

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.900
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:28.860
Master stinky!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.360
Mr. Reiji, did you skip your bath again?

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.570
I took one! Right, Noela?

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:38.300
<i>Later, "Beast-Be-Gone" became</i>

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:41.580
<i>incredibly popular among 
farmers troubled by pesky beasts.</i>

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:46.460
<i>But while I was making this medicine, 
Noela refused to come near me.</i>

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.050
This kind of hurts my feelings.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:50.880
You stink!

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:54.990
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 3
Capshin Fluid</b>

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:55.220
Woof, woof.

00:15:57.050 --> 00:16:00.590
Good morning, Captain—
I mean, Ms. Annabelle.

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:02.640
Good morning, R-Reiji.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:04.430
You're here for your usual?

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:07.060
Actually, could you make it ten today?

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:08.200
I'll pay fer the extras.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.860
Y-Yeah, sure. Noela?

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:11.820
Woof!

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:15.280
You really do love your potions.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:15.280
Thanks.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.040
Woof.

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:16.740
Thank you.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:19.240
Delicious, delicious!

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:22.420
It ain't me who's been drinkin' 'em recently.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.700
In any case, thanks for everythin'.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:29.060
Excuse us... Oh, Captain.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:29.630
Captain.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:31.970
Doz, Moz, what are you doin' here?

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:33.210
Nothin'.

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:37.240
You didn't come here to discuss 
anythin' fishy with Reiji, did you?

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:38.320
But Captain—

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:41.810
No buts! The apothecary's 
got nothin' to do with this!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:45.520
Um, if there's anything I can do, 
I'd be happy to help.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.730
Thank you. We knew you'd help us...

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.450
Medicine god!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.820
Seriously, please stop calling me that!

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:55.030
Then allow us to call you 
"Brother," Brother Reiji!

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.110
Brother Reiji!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.740
<i>I guess it's better than being called a god.</i>

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:02.700
Are you aware that many bandits 
have been comin' to Kalta recently?

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:06.580
I'll explain the situation.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.840
People were injured protecting 
the town against bandits?

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.400
Yup. They're pretty tough.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:18.310
So the captain's been givin' 
her potions to the injured.

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:20.050
Don't mention that.

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:24.230
But unless we get those bandits 
back, the lord will stop payin' us.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.060
We'll have to find another job.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:29.190
After all, we're just mercenaries.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.650
So that's why you came to me.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.770
Yeah. We came to you, Brother Reiji.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:35.860
We were hopin' to pick yer brain.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:38.780
I sense a fight. I'll protect you, Master.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.650
Ms. Noela, why don't you come 
over here and help me make lunch?

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.700
Woof. Lunch, lunch.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:48.900
Protect, huh? That beast girl is right.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.250
We're supposed to be protectin' you.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.910
We can't ask for yer help.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.760
Don't say that.

00:17:56.170 --> 00:18:00.750
We're able to live like this 
because of your brigade.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.760
Let me help you at least a little.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.630
The medicine god has descended!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:07.800
I told you, I'm not a god.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:08.230
Woof.

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:10.650
I can't stop crying.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.020
Cutting onions makes you cry.

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:15.940
<i>Tears? That's it!</i>

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:20.140
Mr. Doz and Mr. Moz, could you bring me 
the highest proof liquor you can find?

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.450
Of course. We'll bring you whatever 
offerings you want, medicine god.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.600
You're a drinker, too, huh?

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.000
You, too, huh?

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.490
I'm going to use it to make medicine.

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:31.880
Hurry, please.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.010
As you wish.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:37.550
Reiji, is there anythin' I can do?

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.260
Thank you. In that case...

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:43.600
<b>Capshin Peppers</b>

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:48.300
That's the stuff. Could I use those?
I'll buy you more later.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.220
That's fine by me. Is this for your medicine?

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.210
Yeah. Ms. Annabelle, could you come with me?

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:53.120
S-Sure.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:54.320
I'll go with you!

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:56.310
It's better if you don't come again.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.250
So this is how you make 
your medicines. I see.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:11.010
<i>It's hard to work with someone watching me.</i>

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:14.570
Mr. Reiji, Mr. Doz has returned.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:16.570
Got it. Show him in.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:17.730
Okay.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:20.430
This is the strongest stuff I could find.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:22.740
Drinking a glass of this on a cold day...

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:25.310
...and then going to sleep is our greatest joy.

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:27.030
Yeah, I'm not going to drink this, 
so I don't need your anecdotes.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:28.470
As you wish.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.000
<b>Capshin Fluid</b>

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.000
Okay, it's done.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:52.590
Brother Reiji, what...

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:53.360
...is this?

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:55.080
Wait, don't get too close!

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.810
My eyes! My eyes!

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:02.980
You two sure do love to overreact.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:04.800
This water is nothin'.

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.750
It's just a mixture of 
liquor and capshin pepper.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:10.610
And you call yerselves members 
of the Red Cat Brigade.

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:14.770
I can't believe warriors who fight on the 
front lines are writhing in agony over—

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.770
I wouldn't get too close to that.

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:17.110
What is this?!

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:18.960
My eyes! My eyes!

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:22.730
Ow, ow, ow!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.480
I told you not to get close.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:28.130
My eyes! My eyes!

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:29.540
Ow, ow! What is this?!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:30.920
Crap, crap, crap!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.000
Mina, Master's rolling on the floor. 
Everyone's rolling on the floor.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.450
That's Mr. Reiji's job.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:41.240
Come on, let's serve lunch.

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:42.300
Woof.

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:45.300
Thanks for the food. It was good.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.650
I helped Mina cook.

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:48.510
That's right.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:50.030
Captain, we should get going.

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:51.270
Get going.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.550
I know.

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:54.480
Then I'll get your medicine.

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:56.400
Doz, you carry it.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.940
Moz, you carry it.

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:01.100
Who, me? Brother Doz, you're older than me.

00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:02.230
You should carry it.

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:04.930
As our leader, the captain should carry it.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.700
Uh, but I...

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.530
Captain, didn't you say what belongs 
to the Red Cat Brigade is yours,

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.910
and what's yours is yours, too?

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.460
Well, actually, uh...

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:14.460
So you should carry it, Captain!

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:19.570
<i>In the end, Mr. Doz and Mr. Moz took 
turns carrying the capshin fluid.</i>

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:21.880
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.290
<i>It goes without saying</i>

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:27.730
<i>that several days later, 
the bandits fled Kalta screaming.</i>

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.430
<b>Closing Time</b>

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:31.850
Kirio Drugstore.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.020
Thank you...

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.980
...for visiting...

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:37.360
...again today.

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:38.860
Woof.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.640
Demon King.

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:46.860
I acquired this in the human town.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:49.320
It's a new kind of medicine.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:53.290
Oh? So this is the medicine 
everyone's been talking about.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:58.210
This won't do.

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:01.220
This won't do at all.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:04.920
<b>Next Customer</b>

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:03.980
The banquet will be ruined.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Illustration by: Crescent @crescent_D</b>
